y</text><line x1='24' y1='270' x2='24.0' y2='255.6' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='21.0' y='254.6' fill='#64748b' font-size='10'>z</text><g transform='translate(56.0,292)'><rect x='0' y='-8' width='12' height='9' fill='#8b5cf6' fill-opacity='.4' stroke='#7c3aed'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>plano</text></g><g transform='translate(106.5,292)'><line x1='0' y1='-4' x2='14' y2='-4' stroke='#2563eb' stroke-width='2'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>recta</text></g><g transform='translate(157.0,292)'><circle cx='6' cy='-4' r='3.8' fill='#e8487a'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>puntos</text></g></svg><p class='mut' style='font-size:.8rem;margin:.2rem 0;text-align:center'>Figura interactiva: arrástrala para girarla en 3D.</p></div><div class='res'>\\(9x-2y-5z-49=0\\)</div></div>"}],"clasificacion":[{"tema":"geom","tipo":"pos","apartados":"a"},{"tema":"geom","tipo":"ecs","apartados":"b"}],"origen":{"documento":"MAT-2006-RESERVA_4.pdf"},"dificultad":null,"etiquetas":[],"revision":"borrador"},{"id":"matematicas-2006-reserva-4-5","n":5,"num":1,"bloque":"Opción B","puntos":"2,5","enunciado":{"intro":"Sea \\(f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R\\) la función definida por \\(f(x)=\\dfrac{x^2-x+1}{x^2+x+1}\\).","apartados":["(0,75 p.) Estudia si existen y calcula, cuando sea posible, las asíntotas de la gráfica de \\(f\\).","(1,25 p.) Determina los intervalos de crecimiento y decrecimiento, los extremos relativos y los valores que alcanza en ellos la función \\(f\\).","(0,5 p.) Esboza la gráfica de \\(f\\)."]},"solucion":[{"titulo":"Apartado a","html":"<div class='ex'><p>\\(x^2+x+1\\gt0\\) siempre: no hay verticales. \\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\pm\\infty}f(x)=1\\): horizontal \\(y=1\\) (y no hay oblicuas).</p><div class='res'>Asíntota horizontal \\(y=1\\)</div></div>"},{"titulo":"Apartado b","html":"<div class='ex'><p>Estudiamos el signo de \\(f'\\)<i class='n' data-t='tp'>Dentro de cada intervalo la derivada no cambia de signo, así que basta sustituir un valor cualquiera del intervalo para conocer su signo.</i>:</p>\\[f'(x)=\\frac{(2x-1)(x^2+x+1)-(x^2-x+1)(2x+1)}{(x^2+x+1)^2}=\\frac{2x^2-2}{(x^2+x+1)^2}=0\\iff\\boxed{x=\\pm1}\\]<div class='rs' style='overflow-x:auto;margin:.35rem 0'><svg viewBox='0 0 274 108' width='100%' style='max-width:329px;display:block;margin:auto' font-family='system-ui,sans-serif' font-size='14.5' fill='currentColor'><path d='M14 52H260' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.6'/><path d='M96 46V58' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.6'/><text x='96' y='76' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='700'>−1</text><path d='M178 46V58' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.6'/><text x='178' y='76' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='700'>1</text><text x='29.0' y='22' text-anchor='middle' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='#17a673'>+</text><path d='M43.0 40L79.0 10' stroke='#17a673' stroke-width='2' fill='none'/><path d='M70.0 11L79.0 10L77.0 19' stroke='#17a673' stroke-width='2' fill='none'/><text x='55.0' y='99' text-anchor='middle'><tspan font-style='italic' font-family='Georgia,serif'>f</tspan>′(−2) &gt; 0</text><text x='111.0' y='22' text-anchor='middle' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='#e8487a'>−</text><path d='M125.0 10L161.0 40' stroke='#e8487a' stroke-width='2' fill='none'/><path d='M152.0 39L161.0 40L159.0 31' stroke='#e8487a' stroke-width='2' fill='none'/><text x='137.0' y='99' text-anchor='middle'><tspan font-style='italic' font-family='Georgia,serif'>f</tspan>′(0) &lt; 0</text><text x='193.0' y='22' text-anchor='middle' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='#17a673'>+</text><path d='M207.0 40L243.0 10' stroke='#17a673' stroke-width='2' fill='none'/><path d='M234.0 11L243.0 10L241.0 19' stroke='#17a673' stroke-width='2' fill='none'/><text x='219.0' y='99' text-anchor='middle'><tspan font-style='italic' font-family='Georgia,serif'>f</tspan>′(2) &gt; 0</text></svg></div><p>\\(f\\) crece en \\((-\\infty,-1)\\) y \\((1,+\\infty)\\) debido a que \\(f'(x)\\gt0\\), y decrece en \\((-1,1)\\) debido a que \\(f'(x)\\lt0\\)<i class='n' data-t='th'>Si \\(f'\\gt0\\) en un intervalo, \\(f\\) crece en él; si \\(f'\\lt0\\), decrece.</i>. Máximo en \\(x=-1\\): \\(f(-1)=\\frac31=3\\); mínimo en \\(x=1\\): \\(f(1)=\\frac13\\)<i class='n' data-t='why'>Hay un mínimo donde \\(f\\) pasa de decrecer a crecer y un máximo donde pasa de crecer a decrecer.</i>.</p><div class='res'>Crece en \\((-\\infty,-1)\\cup(1,+\\infty)\\), decrece en \\((-1,1)\\). Máximo relativo \\((-1,3)\\); mínimo relativo \\(\\left(1,\\frac13\\right)\\)</div></div>"},{"titulo":"Apartado c","html":"<div class='ex'><div style='overflow-x:auto'><svg viewBox='0 0 300 190' width='100%' style='max-width:380px' font-family='system-ui,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='currentColor'><polyline points='20.0,101.6 21.3,101.4 22.6,101.2 23.9,101.1 25.2,100.9 26.5,100.7 27.8,100.5 29.1,100.3 30.4,100.1 31.7,99.8 33.0,99.6 34.3,99.4 35.6,99.2 36.9,98.9 38.2,98.7 39.5,98.4 40.8,98.2 42.1,97.9 43.4,97.6 44.7,97.4 46.0,97.1 47.3,96.8 48.6,96.5 49.9,96.2 51.2,95.8 52.5,95.5 53.8,95.2 55.1,94.8 56.4,94.5 57.7,94.1 59.0,93.7 60.3,93.3 61.6,92.9 62.9,92.5 64.2,92.1 65.5,91.6 66.8,91.1 68.1,90.7 69.4,90.2 70.7,89.7 72.0,89.1 73.3,88.6 74.6,88.0 75.9,87.4 77.2,86.8 78.5,86.1 79.8,85.5 81.1,84.8 82.4,84.1 83.7,83.3 85.0,82.5 86.3,81.7 87.6,80.9 88.9,80.0 90.2,79.1 91.5,78.1 92.8,77.1 94.1,76.1 95.4,75.0 96.7,73.9 98.0,72.7 99.3,71.4 100.6,70.1 101.9,68.8 103.2,67.3 104.5,65.9 105.8,64.3 107.1,62.7 108.4,61.0 109.7,59.3 111.0,57.5 112.3,55.6 113.6,53.7 114.9,51.8 116.2,49.8 117.5,47.8 118.8,45.8 120.1,43.9 121.4,42.1 122.7,40.3 124.0,38.8 125.3,37.6 126.6,36.7 127.9,36.2 129.2,36.4 130.5,37.1 131.8,38.6 133.1,41.0 134.4,44.2 135.7,48.3 137.0,53.3 138.3,59.0 139.6,65.4 140.9,72.3 142.2,79.4 143.5,86.5 144.8,93.5 146.1,100.2 147.4,106.4 148.7,112.1 150.0,117.3 151.3,121.9 152.6,125.9 153.9,129.3 155.2,132.3 156.5,134.8 157.8,136.9 159.1,138.6 160.4,140.1 161.7,141.2 163.0,142.1 164.3,142.8 165.6,143.4 166.9,143.8 168.2,144.1 169.